From: lojban@googlegroups.com <lojban@googlegroups.com> on behalf of Bruno =
Panasiewicz <ciuak.prog@gmail.com>
Sent: Tuesday, 9 August 2016 7:16 PM
To: mriste
Subject: Re: [lojban] taking action


No offense, but that's a horrible idea. Let me tell you why:

=E2=80=A2 there's no contract or anything, so those who do less while seemi=
ng to do a lot will get the same amount as those who really work hard.

=E2=80=A2 there'd be a need for a lot of money, otherwise it wouldn't gain =
interest.

=E2=80=A2 once the money is gone, the workers are gone.

I think that volunteering is the best choice at this point. I don't want Lo=
jbanistan to be a country of money, but of a great community and a great la=
nguage.

=E2=80=94 mi'e la uakci mu'o

On Aug 9, 2016 8:25 AM, "Timothy Lawrence" <timothy.lawrence@connect.qut.ed=
u.au<mailto:timothy.lawrence@connect.qut.edu.au>> wrote:

I would be more than happy to offer small monetary rewards for community in=
volvement, such as contributing translations, flashcards, stories, poems or=
 diary entries - including from learners. One idea is that a bounty could b=
e given to a random contributor over a week or so. The condition would be t=
hat all work submitted would be with the CC0 content licence or similar.


If anyone knows a system that is good for facilitating something like this,=
 let me know.


I have found https://www.bountysource.com/ but it looks like it needs GitHu=
b or similar (at the moment) which might be a barrier to many possible cont=
ributors. Maybe we could make a hub for all the community projects using a =
supported platform?


I have also found https://www.patreon.com/ but it seems more for regular in=
dividual creators, rather than once-off "competitions". That said, I would =
be interested in supporting some regular contributors in this way too.

I haven't used any of these before but it was just an idea. I am not yet ad=
vanced enough in Lojban to easily contribute directly.

